{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"An Irish UCITS ManCo must exercise substantive oversight—not merely receive reports:\n\n- **Before appointment:** conduct and document proportionate due diligence on each delegate’s competence, authorisation where required, resources, systems, controls, financial standing and conflicts. Establish clear written responsibilities, reporting standards, access/audit rights, subdelegation controls and termination arrangements.\n- **After appointment:** maintain sufficient in-house expertise and resources to supervise effectively. Designated persons must scrutinise and challenge portfolio-management and administration reporting, monitor performance, investment restrictions, risk and compliance, periodically refresh due diligence, and escalate deficiencies to the board. Require remediation and retain the ability to instruct or terminate delegates.\n- **Responsibility retained:** the board and ManCo remain responsible for the delegated functions and regulatory compliance; delegation does not diminish the ManCo’s liability to the UCITS or investors.\n\n**Worth knowing:** outsourcing execution cannot turn the ManCo into a “letter-box” entity.\n\nSources: UCITS Directive, Article 13; Central Bank of Ireland Fund Management Companies Guidance."}}
